      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">c. 1499</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guru-nanak">Guru Nanak</a>’s spiritual experience at the river Bein near Sultanpur Lodhi begins his mission</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1577</span><span class="rf-text">Guru Ram Das founds the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amritsar">Amritsar</a> around its sacred pool</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1604</span><span class="rf-text">Guru Arjan installs the Adi Granth, the Sikh scripture, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-temple">Harmandir Sahib</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amritsar">Amritsar</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1606</span><span class="rf-text">Guru Arjan is executed under the Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jahangir">Jahangir</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1675</span><span class="rf-text">Guru Tegh Bahadur is executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> on the orders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1699</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guru-gobind-singh">Guru Gobind Singh</a> founds the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalsa">Khalsa</a> at Anandpur on the festival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaisakhi">Vaisakhi</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1799</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a> takes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore">Lahore</a> and goes on to found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1984</span><span class="rf-text">The Indian army’s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/operation-blue-star">Operation Blue Star</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-temple">Golden Temple</a>, followed by the assassination of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indira-gandhi">Indira Gandhi</a> and anti-Sikh violence</span></li></ol>
